      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it's hard to see it as \"beautiful\" when it feels so cold. everything is just... transient. like, i work, i try to be a good person, i deal with all this pain, but in a billion years none of that even matters. it's like we're just performing for an empty room. if the universe is just mindless physics and empty space, then why does it feel like we're being forced to suffer through all this just to end up as nothing anyway?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
